# Makes the register citable: GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this file,
# and anyone quoting a verdict can point at a specific dated version rather than "some repo".
# That matters more here than for most projects — this register has been publicly wrong four
# times and corrected itself each time, and a correction only reaches people who can be found.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "token-spread: the strict identity register"
message: "If you cite a verdict from this register, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Angus
    alias: hangryclaude
repository-code: "https://github.com/hangryclaude/token-spread"
abstract: >-
  187 LLM cost-reduction techniques adjudicated against a single question — does the model read a
  different sequence of tokens, does a different model answer, or does a different amount of
  thinking happen? 67 pass, 28 pass on the provider's word alone, 52 are rejected, and 40 are
  unresolved and published as unresolved. The register publishes what it rejected, what it could
  not settle, and its own dated errata, including four entries expelled from the passing column
  when their cited sources failed verification.
keywords:
  - llm
  - inference-cost
  - prompt-caching
  - adjudication
  - reproducibility
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-08-13"
version: "2026.08.13"
